#
# The Loom toolchain the shipped Loom cards were built against (owner direction 2026-11-21, "pure Loom";
# ~/briefs/LOOM-GPU-SWITCH.md, work item L5).
#
# TWO PINS THAT ARE EASY TO CONFLATE, KEPT APART ON PURPOSE:
#
#   * THIS FILE records which hrx-system commit DECLARES the `hrx_loom` version the cards need, and which
#     `hrx-loom-library` catalog commit that same file names.
#   * `third_party/hrx-system` records the runtime the ENGINE compiles against.
#
# They are not the same commit, and today they do not even overlap. Measured 2026-11-21: 314238a81c is NOT an
# ancestor of the engine's hrx-system gitlink 7f4236924aadc, and that gitlink carries no
# loom/packaging/python/version.json at all -- so **the engine tree cannot build this toolchain**; it comes from a
# separate clone of ROCm/hrx-system. That is the state of the switch, not a defect of this file: the cards were
# built with Loom 0.2.0.dev0 and the engine still runs the HRX fallback route (LOOM-GPU-SWITCH.md condition 1).
#
# WHY THE VERSION CANNOT COME FROM PyPI: the cards were built with hrx-loom 0.2.0.dev0 (LOOM-FUN-USE.md: "hrx-loom
# 0.2.0.dev0 (hrx-system 314238a); PyPI only has 0.1.0"), and the box's own toolchain venv measures 0.1.0
# (`~/amd-oss/toolchains/loom/.venv`, 2026-11-21). So `version=` below is satisfiable only by a source build of
# the wheel at this pin, which is what `build=` names.
#
# Move the pin by hand, after the L2 gate for the model set it serves (LOOM-GPU-SWITCH.md condition 2), and check it
# with tools/ci/loom_pin_check.py --check.
repo=ROCm/hrx-system
sha=314238a81c0fadb123e0256e756f852f448c1d40
package=hrx_loom
version=0.2.0.dev0
version_file=loom/packaging/python/version.json
model_catalog_repo=ROCm/hrx-loom-library
model_catalog_sha=dfd67f4ab2333b648274a3fff97baad464878436
# The build is version-sensitive: the repo pins Bazel in `.bazelversion` (9.2.0 at this commit) and the recipe's LTO
# path needs it. Measured 2026-11-21 on strixhalo: `bazel 9.3.2` (what `~/.local/bin/bazel` is) fails ANALYSIS in 23 s with
#   libamdf/tool/amdf-info/linux/BUILD.bazel:15:16: in cc_library rule ...: fail("When using LTO. The feature
#   supports_start_end_lib must be enabled.")
# while the same command with 9.2.0 on PATH proceeds. So a build against another Bazel reports a toolchain mismatch as if it
# were a source defect -- which is why the version is recorded here rather than in a README.
bazel_version=9.2.0
build=iree-bazel-build --config=loom-sdk --config=opt //loom/packaging/python:wheel
require=loom-serve loom-benchmark loom-fetch
